AI Notes:
• Docker is an open platform for developing, deploying, and running applications using containerization.
• It separates applications from infrastructure to speed up software delivery and simplify management.
• Key Docker components include the Docker Engine (daemon, API, CLI), images, containers, volumes, networks, and registries.
• Containers package applications with dependencies for consistent environments and isolation.
• Docker Swarm manages clusters of Docker hosts to maintain desired service states and ensure availability.
